Title      : GSU: one process per clock edge
Project    : fpga-mister (patch for SNES_MiSTer bdcd33c)
Author     : Konstantin Schmidt (mr_pleasant@gmx.de)
Company    : OHRZ
Created    : 2026-10-30
Description:
  Three processes of GSU.vhd (multiplier, ROM and RAM state machines) have
  an asynchronous reset and two clocked branches, "elsif falling_edge(CLK)"
  and "elsif rising_edge(CLK)".  Quartus builds that, Vivado stops at it
  (both clock edges in one process).  Every signal is written in
  one branch only and every variable is used in one branch only, so each
  process becomes two: the reset assignments of a signal go with the branch
  that writes it, the branches are unchanged (moved, not edited).
  Generated by splitting at the process lines 961, 1025, 1296; the
  scratch copy built with it in Vivado (OOC, GSUMap 2937 LUT, 2026-10-30).
